hadiths[13]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22181","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdillah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever swears a sinful oath to cut off thereby the property of a Muslim man will meet Allah the Mighty and Majestic while He is angry with him. Al-Ash'ath said: Concerning me, by Allah, that was. Between me and a Jewish man there was land, and he denied me, so I brought him to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do you have proof. I said: No. He said to the Jew: Swear. I said: O Messenger of Allah, then he will swear and my property will go. So Allah the Exalted revealed: Those who purchase the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price, to the end of the verse."
"22182","Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salm ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ziyad ibn Kulayb, from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He does not thank Allah who does not thank people."
"22183","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Aqil ibn Talhah, from Muslim ibn Haydam, from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a delegation who thought me the best of them. I said: O Messenger of Allah, we claim that you are of us. He said: We are the sons of al-Nadr ibn Kinanah; we do not accuse our mother nor disown our father. He said: Al-Ash'ath used to say: No man who denies Quraysh from al-Nadr ibn Kinanah will be brought to me except I flogged him the prescribed lashing."
"22184","Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Mujalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, al-Ash'ath ibn Qays narrated to us, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the delegation of Kindah. He said to me: Have you a child. I said: A boy was born to me on my way out to you, from the daughter of Jad, and I wished that in his place the people were fed to fullness. He said: Do not say that, for in them is delight of the eye and reward when taken. Then, if you say that, they are cowardly and sorrowful; they are cowardly and sorrowful."
"22185","Ziyad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Tufayl al-Bakka'i narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Abdillah ibn Mas'ud, who said: Whoever swears a binding oath to deserve thereby property while sinful therein will meet Allah while He is angry with him, and its confirmation is in the Quran: Those who purchase the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price, to the end of the verse. He said: Al-Ash'ath came out reciting it. He said: Concerning me this verse was revealed. A man claimed a well of mine, and we disputed to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Your two witnesses, or his oath. I said: If he swears, he will swear sinfully. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever swears a binding oath to deserve thereby property will meet Allah while He is angry with him."
"22186","Waki' narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, who said: Al-Ash'ath ibn Qays entered and said: What does Abu Abd al-Rahman narrate to you. They informed him. Ash'ath said: He spoke truth; concerning me it was revealed. Between me and a man there was a dispute over land, and I disputed with him to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Do you have proof. I said: No. He said: Then his oath. He said: I said: Then he will swear. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever swears a binding oath to cut off thereby the property of a Muslim man while sinful therein will meet Allah the Mighty and Majestic while He is angry with him. He said: Then was revealed: Those who purchase the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price."
"22187","Waki' narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Kurdus, from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Whoever swears a binding oath to cut off thereby the property of a Muslim man while lying therein will meet Allah the Mighty and Majestic maimed."
"22188","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdillah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever swears a false oath to cut off thereby the property of a man, or he said: his brother, will meet Allah the Mighty and Majestic while He is angry with him. Its confirmation was revealed in the Quran: Those who purchase the covenant of Allah and their oaths for a small price, those shall have no share in the Hereafter, to a painful punishment. He said: Al-Ash'ath met me and said: What did Abdillah narrate to you today. He said: I said to him: Such and such. He said: Concerning me it was revealed."
"22189","Bahz and Affan both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Aqil ibn Talhah narrated to me, Affan said in his hadith: I am Aqil ibn Talhah al-Sulami, from Muslim ibn Haydam, from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays, that he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a delegation of Kindah. Affan said: Thinking me the best of them. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, we claim that you are of us. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: We are the sons of al-Nadr ibn Kinanah; we do not accuse our mother nor disown our father. He said: Al-Ash'ath said: By Allah, I hear no one denying Quraysh from al-Nadr ibn Kinanah except I flogged him the prescribed lashing."
"22190","Bahz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Musarrif narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Sharik al-Amiri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Adi al-Kindi, from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The most grateful of people to Allah the Mighty and Majestic are the most grateful of them to people."
"22191","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ibn Shubrumah, from Abu Ma'shar, from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He does not thank Allah who does not thank people."
"22192","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Abdillah ibn Mas'ud, three hadiths. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever cuts off the property of a Muslim man without right will meet Allah the Mighty and Majestic while He is angry with him. He said: Al-Ash'ath ibn Qays came and said: What does Abu Abd al-Rahman narrate to you. He said: We narrated to him. He said: Concerning me was this hadith. I disputed a cousin of mine to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning a well of mine in his hand, and he denied me. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Your proof that it is your well, otherwise his oath. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do I do with his oath; if you make it by his oath, my well will go; my opponent is a sinful man. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever cuts off the property of a Muslim man without right will meet Allah the Mighty and Majestic while He is angry with him. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited: Those who purchase the covenant of Allah, the verse."
"22193","Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Kurdus narrated to us, from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays, that a man of Kindah and a man of Hadramawt disputed to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning land in Yemen. The Hadrami said: O Messenger of Allah, this man and his father seized my land. The Kindi said: O Messenger of Allah, it is my land, I inherited it from my father. The Hadrami said: O Messenger of Allah, make him swear that he does not know it is my land and my father's land which his father seized. The Kindi prepared for the oath. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No servant or man cuts off property by his oath except he will meet Allah on the day he meets Him maimed. The Kindi said: It is his land and his father's land."
